review_comments:
Fair point - this is an older/esoteric piece of kit (Honeywell VisionPro Wifi), never seen one before - an edge case, but it was supported by this integration previously.

I did consider 'withdrawing' support for it, as I don't want to get committed to extensive writing workarounds like this for (maybe) 1-2 users...

This is what the JSON looks like for this kit:
```json
{
    "locationId": "2166142",
    "gateways": [{
            "gatewayId": "395968",
            "temperatureControlSystems": [{
                    "systemId": "416856",
                    "zones": [{
                            "zoneId": "416856",
                            "temperatureStatus": {

```
In all other systems I've seen, the `zoneId` value (416856) is distinct from the `systemId` - this one, they share the same value! This has come to a head due to several issues, one being that the controller and the zone are separate entities and the controller is implemented as a climate entity - hence the need for two unique IDs.

I am satisfied this is a special case, and adding the `z` suffix is a simple fix that will allow this system to behave as all the other evohome-compatible systems.
